  "name": "automatafl-game-server",
  "description": "A high-concurrency game backend implemented in Rust using the Axum web framework and SeaORM for persistent storage. It features a sophisticated state management system with WebSocket-based real-time event broadcasting, integrated matchmaking, and Argon2-secured authentication. The architecture leverages asynchronous task orchestration via Tokio and shared state through DashMap to support low-latency game logic execution and snapshotting.",
